OL,3,ARegulating AI 'not the right place to
OL,4,Astart' says Bailey
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Governor of the Bank of England has
OL,7,Fsaid regulating artificial intelligence
OL,8,F(AI) "is not the right place to start"
OL,9,Fbut instead called first for "rigorous"
OL,10,Ftesting to find vulnerabilities and
OL,11,Fcreate safeguards to contain risk.
OL,13,FWriting his first-ever article for
OL,14,FSubstack, Andrew Bailey said the risks
OL,15,Faround AI were "real and increasingly
OL,16,Fsignificant".
OL,23,APub: 30-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/18
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,107,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11904
SC,0004
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1790794499
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,ARegulating AI 'not the right place to
OL,4,Astart' says Bailey
OL,5,
OL,6,FHe said AI development should not be
OL,7,Fhalted or prohibited - "on the
OL,8,Fcontrary, the benefits are immense" -
OL,9,Fbut added there must be a system for
OL,10,Fintervention and to establish
OL,11,Fboundaries in which AI operates.
OL,13,FThe debate about the potential risks
OL,14,Fsurrounding the rapid development of AI
OL,15,Fand what it means for humanity has
OL,16,Fintensified in recent weeks.
OL,23,APub: 30-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG4/18
